<!--
    angr SAILR / Phoenix goto-reduction via return-tail duplication
    (Basque et al., USENIX Security 2024 "SAILR"; ReturnDuplicator).

    coreutils dd 'argmatch_to_argument' (x86-64, GCC) @ 0x40a640.  A shared
    return tail (`v2 = 0;` falling through to the single `return v2;`) has two
    predecessors (the initial `if (v2 == 0)` true-arm and an in-loop
    `if (v2 == 0)` edge), so Ghidra's CollapseStructure must express the second
    edge as an unstructured `goto label;` (CollapseStructure has no schema that
    duplicates a tail to avoid a goto).  angr emits zero gotos by duplicating the
    constant return tail into the in-loop edge, turning the cross-edge into a
    structured early return.

    Stage model: S8 "goto-quality" sub-stage.  The option-gated
    `ActionGotoReduce` (option `gotoreduce`, default-OFF) runs after
    ActionFinalStructure: it finds `if (cond) goto T` where T is a small
    single-successor basic-block chain ending in `return`, and rewrites it to
    `if (cond) { tail }` (a print-tree copy of the same ops, no p-code cloned and
    def/use untouched), then clears T's now-unused label.

    The bcmp@plt call target (0x402360) is outside this single-function chunk, so
    it renders as an unnamed sub call; that is irrelevant to the goto metric.

    Pass 1 (option gotoreduce off): assertions prove the bug; one `goto label_`
    and the `label_:` definition are present (the residual unstructured edge).
    Pass 2 (option gotoreduce on): the goto and label are gone and the constant
    return tail is duplicated, so the combined `return ` count rises from one
    (pass 1) to three (one in pass 1 plus two in pass 2).
-->
